on chat context.\\n\\nRequired design contract:\\n- Autorouting decision = route(client_inputs, fiz_models_snapshot).\\n- Client inputs include policy/profile, pins, no_remote, metered opt-in, tools/context/reasoning needs, and other explicit constraints.\\n- The fiz models snapshot is the only source of routing facts: health, quota, model availability, effective cost, actual_cash_spend, billing kind, context/tools/reasoning support, locality, reliability, latency, utilization, and per-field freshness.\\n- Server/refresh coordinator owns background freshness and refresh coalescing. fiz models must not spawn independent probe storms.\\n- fiz models is quick; fiz models --refresh blocks on routing-relevant stale fields; fiz models --refresh-all blocks on all refreshable fields. Without a running server, stale output suggests starting the server or using --refresh.\\n- Hard gates are limited to explicit user constraints and dispatchability. Cost, quality, health risk, latency, utilization, and power fit are scoring inputs.\\n- Subscription models use PAYG-equivalent effective/shadow cost for scoring while retaining actual_cash_spend=false. Pay-per-token providers are gated only when dispatch creates actual metered spend and the user has not opted in.\\n\\nIn scope: docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-004-model-routing.md, docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-011-cost-based-routing-with-quota-pools.md, docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-fizeau-service.md, docs/routing/*.md, ADR-012 snapshot/cache docs if present.\\n\\nOut of scope: implementation code; create follow-up beads instead of partially implementing.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. rg -n \u0026#39;route\\(client_inputs, fiz_models_snapshot\\)|actual_cash_spend|effective_cost|PAYG-equivalent|refresh-all|server.*fresh|hard gates\u0026#39; docs/helix docs/routing returns matches in the amended routing/snapshot docs.\\n2. rg -n \u0026#39;subscription.*free|zero-cost subscription|frontier_excluded_by_cheap_policy\u0026#39; docs/helix docs/routing returns no matches.\\n3. ddx doc stale exits 0 or reports only pre-existing unrelated stale documents.\\n4. lefthook run pre-commit --all-files passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:docs, area:routing, area:cache, kind:spec, plan-2026-05-13-snapshot-routing\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-4847c99e\" spec-id=\"FEAT-004\" base-rev=\"521a0c50e6065cd9d1df11f6ec67cdcd69a52546\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260513T175025-e630aa9f\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"FEAT-004\" path=\"docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-004-model-routing.md\"\u003eFeature Specification: FEAT-004 — Shared Model Catalog and Policy Routing\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","attempt_id":"20260513T175025-e630aa9f","base_rev":"521a0c50e6065cd9d1df11f6ec67cdcd69a52546","bead_id":"fizeau-64a85a3d","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260513T175025-e630aa9f","correlation_id":"fizeau-64a85a3d:20260513T175025-e630aa9f","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260513T175025-e630aa9f/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"288b990eca5dcfa8a0af727d9ffda517bdcb37562f9f959fd0e3c9de5e2ad8cf","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-516b4eb1","worker_id":""}}}
